==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|flum}}, from {{der|en|fro|flum}}, {{m|fro|flun}}, from {{der|en|la|flumen}}, from {{m|la|fluere||to flow}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/fluːm/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-flume.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːm|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}
[[File:Hävla_bruk_sågverket.jpg|right|thumb|A log flume in Sweden in 2010.]]

# A [[ravine]] or [[gorge]], usually one with [[water]] running through.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1898|title=Recreation|page=31
|text=Near the upper end of the portage the river falls 100 feet in as many rods, the water going at lightning speed through a natural '''flume''' in the rock. So rapid is the descent that the water in the '''flume''' is but 3 feet deep. We named this the "Devil's Slide."}}
# An open [[channel]] or [[trough]] used to direct or divert [[liquid]]s, especially to carry materials (logs, mined material, etc) or people (as a [[water slide]]), especially (but not always) one where the walls are raised above the surrounding terrain rather than recessed into it like a ditch.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Dale Samuelson|author2=Wendy Yegoiants|title=The American Amusement Park|publisher=Motorbooks International|isbn=9780760309810|page=90
|text=[...] the '''flumes''' are generally not dark rides and they run much faster. Two notable exceptions are the Timber Mountain{{nb...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2012-07-04|author=Susanna Moore|title=The Whiteness of Bones|publisher=Vintage|isbn=9780307826602|page=4
|text={{...}} aqueducts, wooden half-barrels laid on their sides and elevated on rusty trestles, to rush the icy spring water down the mountainside to the fields. This system of irrigation through '''flumes''' was simple, but effective. There were miles of '''flumes''' and, {{...}} the children of the island used the '''flumes''' as water slides. The location of certain especially fast and dangerous '''flumes''' was kept secret in families for generations and passed on in unquestioned solemnity . It was against the law to use the '''flumes''' as water slides{{nb...}} }}

